WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.869
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Hasan Minhaj.

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:05.004
Your special talks about --
the episode of your show

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:08.174
"The Patriot Act," where you
talked about Saudi Arabia

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.576
and the killing of
the journalist Jamaal Khashoggi.

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:12.745
Can you just remind people
a little bit who might not

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:14.480
remember exactly
how that went down?

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.018
-Yeah, so, "Washington Post"
journalist Jamaal Khashoggi went

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:23.356
into a Saudi embassy,
got murdered, not good.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:26.592
-Nope.
-Had a very hot take on my show

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:29.162
"Patriot Act" -- you know,
murder is bad.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.830
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.331
Saudi Arabia didn't like that.

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:33.565
They banned the episode.

00:00:33.565 --> 00:00:35.201
-Right, so this was --

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.303
You could not stream it
in Saudi Arabia.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:41.974
-Okay. I am a practicing Muslim
and I come to find out

00:00:41.974 --> 00:00:46.212
I violated their cybercrime law
and I was sentenced to

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.080
five years in Saudi prison.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.017
I know. I've always wanted to be
an international villain.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.651
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.651 --> 00:00:54.654
It's been a dream of mine.

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:56.655
I just didn't want to be
for the dorkiest [bleep] ever.

00:00:56.655 --> 00:01:01.093
But I then found out
my Hajj visa was denied.

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:04.364
So, Muslims around the world,
once in our life,

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:07.333
we have to make our pilgrimage
to Mecca --

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.969
not Madison Square Garden,
the real Mecca.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:11.537
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:13.105
And I was denied.

00:01:13.105 --> 00:01:15.808
And it really, like, hurt me,

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:18.878
this big part of my faith
I now can't complete.

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:22.748
But God is pretty amazing, and
he has this loophole for Muslims

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:26.252
that if you can't complete
your pilgrimage,

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.788
someone can make it
on your behalf.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:31.891
So I called Nathan Fielder.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.026
-Good call.

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.360
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.096
-Because we know
he's committed to bits.

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:38.598
-That's a real good bit.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:44.170
-And I go, "Nate, I know you're
committed to comedy."

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.273
Have you ever thought of
committing yourself to Islam?"

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.741
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:52.111
And we had this bit where there
was like my emam I grew up with.

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:54.881
"He's here. You can just accept
the one true faith.

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:57.883
And you can go to Mecca,
make your pilgrimage, come back,

00:01:57.883 --> 00:01:59.351
we'll do an episode about that.

00:01:59.351 --> 00:02:02.188
It will be this amazing
spiritual cheat code."

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:04.590
And Nate, I could see him
just kind of doing the math,

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.292
and he goes,
"That's really funny."

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:09.028
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:10.363
"Would this get me killed?"

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:12.498
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:16.368
And I go, "Nate, I have
a question for you.

00:02:16.368 --> 00:02:18.171
How committed are you to
comedy?"

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:19.506
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.273
"Because everyone says
you're a genius."

00:02:21.273 --> 00:02:23.376
How funny would it be if I --
Well, it's not funny.

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:26.745
But if he did die...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.745 --> 00:02:28.748
...and then I accepted the Emmy
on his behalf.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:31.984
[ Laughter ]
And I was like, "Nathan Fielder

00:02:31.984 --> 00:02:36.189
died doing what he loved --
converting to Islam."

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.458
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:42.528
-Yeah, that would have been
special television.

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:45.631
Do people still -- I imagine
people still talk to you,

00:02:45.631 --> 00:02:46.866
ask you about Saudi Arabia
all the time.

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.100
-All the time. Yeah.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.802
I'm like, "Why?" I mean,
I'm dressed like the flag.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.071
But --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:54.307
So, Adam Levine DMed me.
-Okay.

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:56.409
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:59.011
-Not like that, not like that,
not like that, not like that.

00:02:59.011 --> 00:03:01.247
Not like that, okay?
-Definitely not the answer

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.115
I was expecting.
-Okay.

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:07.854
So, a year ago, he DMs me
and he goes, "Hey, can we talk?"

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:12.658
And I go, "Yeah,"
and I call him, and he goes,

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:14.894
"Should I perform
in Saudi Arabia?"

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:17.430
Like, all of a sudden,
I'm the Middle East expert.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.965
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:20.966
And he goes, "They're offering
me a lot of money.

00:03:20.966 --> 00:03:23.002
Should I go do it?"

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.470
And I didn't know what to do,

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.438
so I called one of
my comedy mentors.

00:03:26.438 --> 00:03:28.174
I'm a Padawan,
he's a comedy Jedi.

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:29.609
I go, "What do I tell
Adam Levine?"

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:32.211
He goes, "Okay, well,
just ask him,

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:33.713
'Do you really need the money?'"

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:35.081
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.216
"If not, you should probably,
like, stand up for what

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:39.986
you believe, and, you know,
move forward that way."

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.754
And I gave Adam Levine
this huge speech.

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:44.624
I'm like, "If you don't need the
money, Adam, stand up for what

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:47.193
you believe
and do the right thing.

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:48.761
I hope to hear from you soon."

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:50.296
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:53.632
And then a few weeks ago, I was
on stage, I was just working on

00:03:53.632 --> 00:03:56.436
material and Beena was backstage
and she goes "Oh, my God,

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:58.304
did you hear about Adam Levine?"

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:01.541
And I look at my phone,
and I'm like, "Oh, thank God."

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:03.542
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:04.944
"He's just a pervert."

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:08.681
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:11.183
-Thank God.
-At least he's not a sellout.

00:04:11.183 --> 00:04:13.152
-Kind of all in, yeah.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.286
Hey, thanks so much
for being here.

00:04:14.286 --> 00:04:16.956
Congrats on the special.
Hasan Minhaj, everybody.

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.858
"The King's Jester"
is streaming now on Netflix.

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.393
We'll be right back
with Tony Hale.

